    "q-213261": {
      "dom_id": "step-q213261",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14120255/assets/ded4e8a94730585809c5534fee8d401481c919d529a67cd088e96b8797f2b237.png)\n\nThe directed graph of a relation defined on the set ${2,5,8}$ is given above. Which of the following ordered pairs belong to the relation?\n\n- $(2,2)$\n- $(2,8)$\n- $(8,5)$",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation can be visualized using a directed graph (digraph), where \n\n- the nodes (vertices) of the graph are elements of the underlying set,\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines an arrow from node $x$ to node $y$,\n\n- each pair $(x,x)$ from the relation defines a loop from node $x$ to itself.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given ordered pairs.\n\n- The pair $(2,2)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the directed graph has a loop from the node $2$ to itself.\n\n- The pair $(2,8)$ does not belong to the relation since the directed graph does not have an arrow that starts at the node $2$ and ends at the node $8.$\n\n- The pair $(8,5)$ belongs to the relation. Indeed, the directed graph has an arrow that starts at the node $8$ and ends at the node $5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-213261-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I and III only",
              "html": "I and III only"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-213261-b",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "I only",
              "html": "I only"
            },
            {
              "option": "c",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-213261-c",
              "type": "text",
